.TH EXECUTE 1 "October 2026" "execute 0.9.0-rc.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
execute \- readable Unix workflows with declarative applets and direct pipes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B execute
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARG\fR...]
.br
.B execute
.B check|explain|inspect|run
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B execute resume
.I FILE
.B \-\-checkpoint
.I DIR
.br
.B execute applets
.BR list|inspect|discover|match
.br
.B execute modules
.BR inspect|verify|lock
.I MANIFEST
.br
.B execute service generate
.BR systemd|launchd
.I FILE
.br
.B execute lsp
.RB [ \-\-stdio ]
.br
.B execute live
.IR SUBCOMMAND ...
.br
.B execute model
.BR classify|judge|score|generate|extract
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute runs
.I .program
files: typed glue that starts native commands and manifest applets, moves their
output through direct pipes, and reports what it will do. Computation belongs to
applets, not to the language. Use
.B execute check
to validate a program without running anything, and
.B execute explain
to see the effects a program would have.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check \fIFILE\fR
Validate a program without running it. Add
.B \-\-json
for a structured result.
.TP
.B explain \fIFILE\fR
Show each step and its declared effects. Add
.B \-\-json
for a machine-readable plan, which includes the declared flags and options.
.TP
.B inspect \fIFILE\fR
Describe the program's inputs, including flags, options and their sources, without
running it.
.TP
.B run \fIFILE\fR
Run the program. Arguments after
.B \-\-
are passed to the program's declared inputs. Use
.B run \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\- \-\-help\fR
for the help generated from its declarations.
.TP
.B resume \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\-checkpoint\fR \fIDIR\fR
Continue a checkpointed run from its last durable step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input " NAME=VALUE"
Supply a declared program input. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Structured result for
.B check
and
.BR explain .
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest\-dir " DIR"
Directory containing applet manifests. Defaults to the installed manifests.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest\-catalog " FILE"
Packed manifest catalog. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-manifest\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-capability\-policy " FILE"
Enforce a versioned applet policy for
.BR check ", " explain ", " inspect ", " run ", " resume ", " live .
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-flow\-policy " FILE"
Enforce origin and persistence data-flow grants.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " DIR"
Cache directory for
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.BI \-\-checkpoint " DIR"
Durable checkpoint directory for
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.B \-\-retry\-uncertain
Retry an invocation whose prior outcome is uncertain. Only with
.BR resume .
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Print execution details to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-output\-bytes " N"
Largest captured output, in bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-command\-timeout\-ms " N"
Lifetime limit for each native pipeline.
.TP
.BI \-\-total\-timeout\-ms " N"
Lifetime limit for the whole workflow.
.TP
.BI \-\-drain\-timeout\-ms " N"
Budget for an interrupt to finish running work before the run is cancelled. Default
10000. Only with
.BR run .
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the command help, or with a program file and
.B \-\-
the program's generated help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
A program's explicit
.B exit with status
value is its exit status. A failing native command reports its own status. An
interrupt exits with 130 after any drain.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/manifests
Bundled applet manifests, found from the installed binary's location.
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/docs
Language and platform documentation.
.TP
.I /usr/share/execute/editors
Editor grammar for syntax highlighting.
.SH SEE ALSO
The language reference in
.IR /usr/share/execute/docs .
.SH AUTHORS
Execute maintainers. Source:
.UR https://github.com/monstercameron/NextGenScriptingLanguage
.UE
